Part A : Cora is a citation network:

2708 nodes — each node is a scientific paper
5429 edges — citations between papers
1433 node features — bag-of-words representation of paper content
7 classes — the research topic/category of each paper
Task: Semi-supervised node classification (only 140 labeled nodes for training)

Part B : Recall Steps in standard transformer model :

1. Embedding
2. Attention over all embeddings(Self-attention) over multiple heads
3. MLP
4. Unembedding

Part C :

1. LapPE (Laplacian Positional Encoding)
2. InputProjection    — linear map from node_features → d_model
3. GraphAttention     — neighbor-masked multi-head attention
4. TransformerLayer   — Attention + FFN + LayerNorm + Residual
5. GraphTransformer   — stack of layers + classifier head
6. Training Loop      — on Cora with Adam optimizer

Part D :

Architecture :

Input Node Features [N x 1433]
         │
         ▼
  Linear Projection (Embedding)
  [N x d_model]
         │
         ▼
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│    Graph Transformer Layer  │  (×L layers)
│                             │
│  ┌───────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Multi-Head Attention │  │
│  │  (Approach 1 :           |
|   buidling global attention)|
| (Approach 2 : implementing  |
|   over neighbors only)      |
| (Approach 3 : global        |
|   attention with sparcity)  |         
│  └───────────────────────┘  │
│            │                │
│       Add & Norm            │
│            │                │
│  ┌───────────────────────┐  │
│  │    Feed Forward (MLP) │  │
│  └───────────────────────┘  │
│            │                │
│       Add & Norm            │
└─────────────────────────────┘
         │
         ▼
  Linear Classifier Head
  [N x 7]
         │
         ▼
     Softmax → Class Prediction

Part E:

The Core: Graph Multi-Head Attention
This is the heart of the model. For each node i, attention is computed only over its neighbors j ∈ N(i):
Step-by-step:

1. Project node features into Q, K, V
Q = X · W_Q     # What am I looking for?
K = X · W_K     # What do I offer?
V = X · W_V     # What value do I carry?

2. Compute attention scores (neighbor-masked)
e_ij = (Q_i · K_j^T) / √(d_k)    # only for j ∈ neighbors of i(Depending on the approach)

3. Normalize with softmax over neighbors
α_ij = softmax over j∈N(i) of e_ij

4. Aggregate neighbor values
h_i = Σ α_ij · V_j

5. Multi-head: run H parallel attention heads, then concat + project
h_i = Concat(head_1, ..., head_H) · W_O

Part F:

How is it different from vallina Transformers?

Feature             | Vanilla Transformer    | Graph Transformer

Attention scope     | All tokens (global)    | Only neighbors (local)
Positional encoding | Sequential positions   | Graph structure (e.g., Laplacian PE)
Input               | Sequence               | Graph(nodes + edges)
Masking             | Causal or padding mask | Adjacency-based mask

Part G:

Positional Encoding on Graphs:
Since graphs have no natural sequence order, we use Laplacian Eigenvector Positional Encoding (LapPE):

Compute the normalized graph Laplacian: L = I - D^(-1/2) A D^(-1/2)
Take the k smallest non-trivial eigenvectors
Append them to node features as positional signals

This gives nodes a sense of their position/role in the graph topology.

Part H:

Cora Graph
  ├── Node features X: [2708, 1433]
  ├── Adjacency A: [2708, 2708] (sparse)
  └── Labels Y: [2708]

X → [2708, d_model]          # input projection
  + LapPE → [2708, d_model]  # add positional encoding

For each GT layer:
  Neighbor-masked MHA → residual → LayerNorm
  FFN → residual → LayerNorm

Final [2708, d_model] → Linear → [2708, 7] → log_softmax

Part I:

Key Hyper-parameters : 

1. d_model : 64 or 128
2. num_heads : 4 or 8
3. num_layers : 4 
4. dropout : 0.6
5. lr : 0.005
6. epochs : 200
7. k(LapPE dims) : 8